How can I format and print the current date and time in the format "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss" using Java code? Can you explain how the SimpleDateFormat class works and provide examples of different formats that can be used?
To format and print the current date and time in the desired format, you can use the SimpleDateFormat class in Java. Here's an example code snippet:
Date currentDate = new Date();
SimpleDateFormat dateFormat = new SimpleDateFormat("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss");
String formattedDate = dateFormat.format(currentDate);
System.out.println("Formatted date: " + formattedDate);
The output of this code will be the current date and time in the format "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss".
The SimpleDateFormat class allows you to specify different patterns to format dates and times in various ways. For example, if you want to format the date as "MM/dd/yyyy", you can use the pattern "MM/dd/yyyy" instead. Here's an example:
SimpleDateFormat dateFormat = new SimpleDateFormat("MM/dd/yyyy");
String formattedDate = dateFormat.format(currentDate);
System.out.println("Formatted date: " + formattedDate);
This will print the current date in the format "MM/dd/yyyy".

